<!-- ══ ABOUT ════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section" id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Quality is a discipline,<br>not an <em>afterthought</em></h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I'm an aspiring <strong>Software QA Engineer</strong> from Sri Lanka, currently reading for a
            BSc (Hons) in Computer Science with Applied Artificial Intelligence at Coventry University
            via NIBM. My focus is software testing, test case design, defect identification, and the
            quality assurance practices that keep releases predictable.
          </p>
          <p>
            Before QA, I interned at <strong>Arimac</strong> as a Software Engineer &amp; UI/UX
            Engineer, contributing frontend development and interface design to client products
            including Sampath Bank, Hutch, Siddhify, and SherlockAI — alongside freelance
            full-stack work. That background is my advantage: I know how software is built, where
            it tends to break, and how to write a defect report a developer can actually act on.
          </p>
          <p>
            I'm detail-oriented and genuinely curious — the kind of person who reads the edge case in
            the requirements document and asks what happens when the input is empty.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="facts">
          <span class="fact"><i class="fas fa-location-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i> Sri Lanka</span>
          <span class="fact"><i class="fas fa-graduation-cap" aria-hidden="true"></i> BSc (Hons) in progress</span>
          <span class="fact"><i class="fas fa-users" aria-hidden="true"></i> IEEE student member</span>
          <span class="fact fact--live"><i class="fas fa-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i> Open to work</span>
        </div>

        <div class="about-actions">
          <a href="assets/cv/NiragiKodagoda_CV.pdf" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <i class="fas fa-file-arrow-down" aria-hidden="true"></i> Download résumé
          </a>
          <a href="#contact" class="btn btn-ghost">
            <i class="fas fa-paper-plane" aria-hidden="true"></i> Get in touch
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pillars reveal-group">
        <article class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-ico"><i class="fas fa-vial-circle-check" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
          <h3>What I do</h3>
          <p>Manual and functional testing, test case design, and defect reporting that helps teams ship software that behaves as specified.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-ico"><i class="fas fa-magnifying-glass" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
          <h3>How I work</h3>
          <p>Requirements first. I understand intended behaviour before I test, so the defects I raise are real defects — not misread specs.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-ico"><i class="fas fa-code" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
          <h3>Developer's eye</h3>
          <p>Frontend and full-stack build experience means I can reproduce issues precisely and describe them in terms developers can debug.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-ico"><i class="fas fa-bullseye" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
          <h3>Where I'm going</h3>
          <p>Growing into a QA engineering role where I can deepen my automation skills and take ownership of test coverage on a real product.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


